<p>
  The board is a <code>Y.Map</code> named <code>shapes</code>. Each note is a
  nested <code>Y.Map</code> with x, y, text, and color, keyed by a random id.
  Double-click the board to add a note, drag it by the strip along its top, and
  click inside it to type. Each pointer move writes x and y in one transaction,
  so the other window sees the note move while you drag.
</p>
<p>
  A note's text is a plain string, so if two people type in the same note at
  once, the last write wins. To merge concurrent typing, a field needs a
  <code>Y.Text</code>, as in the Code demo.
</p>
